      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C2 is a 100nF capacitor connected between the +5V rail and GND. The +5V rail is the output of U1, an LM1117-5.0 linear regulator.",
      "expected": "The LM1117-5.0 datasheet requires a minimum output capacitance of 10µF (tantalum) for stability. A 100nF capacitor is insufficient and may cause the regulator to oscillate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "C2 | 100nF | Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric | Device:C_Small | Unpolarized capacitor, small symbol"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U1 | LM1117-5.0 | Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-223-3_TabPin2 | fan_controller-rescue:LM1117-5.0-Regulator_Linear"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V : C2.1(passive) J3.1(Pin_1,passive) J4.2(VCC,passive) J6.2(Pin_2,passive) R3.1(passive) U1.2(VO,power_out) U2.8(VCC,power_in) U3.8(VCC,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V rail may oscillate or be unstable, affecting the MCU and other 5V components.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R4", "R6", "D1"],
      "pins": ["R4.1", "R4.2", "R6.1", "R6.2", "D1.1", "D1.2"],
      "nets": ["TACH", "/TACH_IN", "VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "R6 (10K pull-up) is connected between VCC and TACH. R4 (1K series) is between TACH and /TACH_IN. D1 (5V1 Zener) is on TACH. The pull-up is therefore on the MCU side of the series resistor.",
      "expected": "For an open-collector tach signal, the pull-up should be on the fan side of the series resistor (i.e., between VCC and /TACH_IN) so that when the fan pulls low, the MCU input is pulled to 0V through the series resistor. With the current arrangement, the MCU sees a voltage divider (VCC * 1K / (10K + 1K)) when the fan pulls low, which may not be a valid logic low for all VCC values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "TACH : D1.1(K,passive) R4.1(passive) R6.2(passive) U2.3(XTAL2/PB4,bidirectional) U3.3(PB4,bidirectional)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/TACH_IN : J2.3(Pin_3,passive) R4.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "VCC : C1.1(passive) J5.2(Pin_2,passive) JP1.2(B,passive) Q1.2(S,passive) R1.1(passive) R6.1(passive) U1.3(VI,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The tach input may not read low correctly, causing unreliable fan speed measurement.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains two anomalies: the LM1117-5.0 output capacitor C2 is only 100nF instead of the required 10µF, risking regulator instability; and the tach input pull-up R6 is on the wrong side of the series resistor R4, degrading the logic low level seen by the MCU."
}

